      },
      "worked": "Each group contains $12\\div4=3$ people. Choose successive groups of three, then divide by $4!$ because ordering the four groups does not change the grouping.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{\\binom{12}{3}\\binom{9}{3}\\binom{6}{3}\\binom{3}{3}}{4!}\\\\N&=\\frac{220\\times84\\times20\\times1}{24}\\\\N&=15400.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
